        <entry>
          <string>Description</string>
          <string>This combinational circuit determines the highest-scoring category across four 17-bit parallel channels using a two-tiered binary 
elimination tree. Subtractor units calculate differences ($A - B$) to evaluate wins via their sign bits. Multiplexers route winning 
intermediate scores and matching identity tags forward, ultimately outputting the final 2-bit winning class index.</string>
        </entry>
      </elementAttributes>
      <pos x="-140" y="0"/>
    </visualElement>
